From: VyOS ARM64 Builder maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: rockchip: distinguish deferred regulator acquisition

The Orange Pi GPU/NPU supplies can become available after the power-domain
controller. Preserve the error and retry path, but use dev_err_probe so that
-EPROBE_DEFER is debug-level and real supply errors remain errors.
Local adaptation of the kernel's dev_err_probe convention; no power sequencing
or Device Tree changes. Build and next-boot validation required.

--- a/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
@@ -687,10 +687,9 @@
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = rockchip_pd_regulator_enable(pd);
-	if (ret) {
-		dev_err(pd->pmu->dev, "Failed to enable supply: %d\n", ret);
-		return ret;
-	}
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(pd->pmu->dev, ret,
+				     "Failed to enable power-domain supply\n");
 
 	ret = rockchip_pd_power(pd, true);
 	if (ret)
